BT /F1 11 Tf 50 700 Td (Plants harness solar energy to manufacture sugars from carbon dioxide and water. This biological mechanism, carried out in chloroplasts via the pigment chlorophyll, releases oxygen as a by-product. The general reaction combines six molecules of CO2 with six of H2O, producing one glucose molecule and six oxygen molecules. Without this process, atmospheric oxygen levels would collapse and most food webs would disintegrate, since producers form their nutritional foundation.) Tj ET
